b with a pacifier that was attached to the clothing with a clip-on strap. An 10 month old child was observed sleeping in a play yard with a blanket. These are prohibited items for children under 12 months of age. The provider corrected this during the inspection by removing the blanket and pacifier strap.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026239226","violation_type_title":"AP Cribs - Only Snug Fitting Sheet and Crib Mattress Cover Allowed if Infant Younger than 12 Months of Age (26 TAC §747.2315(b))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1439212-i20241029-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-2326-a-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1439212-i20241029","date":"2024-10-29","original_code":"747.2326(a)(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-07","finding":"Infant May Not Sleep in a Restrictive Device - Remove the infant from the device and place the infant in a crib as soon as possible: A child was observed to be sleeping in a bouncy seat which is a restrictive device.  A caregiver was sitting on the couch in front of the sleeping child.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026279007","violation_type_title":"Infant May Not Sleep in a Restrictive Device - Remove the infant from the device and place the infant in a crib as soon as possible (26 TAC §747.2326(a)(2))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1439212-i20241029-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-1303-5-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1439212-i20241029","date":"2024-10-29","original_code":"747.1303(5)(A)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-07","finding":"Training Requirements for Primary Caregiver -30 Hours Annual Training: The Primary Caregiver lacked 1.5 hours in annual training including the required training for understanding building and physical premises safety.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026